{"text": "I ran out of steps before I could complete the design, so here is an honest status report rather than a design.\n\n## What I did\n\n1. **Read the project files** \u2014 `GEMINI_Hackathon_Challenge_Requirements.pdf`, `GEMINI_Heating_Demand_Daily_2027.csv` (365 daily rows, `date,heating_demand_MWth`), `GEMINI_Cooling_Demand_Daily_2027.csv` (365 daily rows, `date,cooling_demand_MWcool`).\n2. **Tried to fill the case from the files** with `set_case(files=[...], columns={...: {'date': 'time'}}, changes=...)`, time axis 2027-01-01 \u2192 2027-12-31 at a 1-day step, heating and cooling power series bound to the two CSVs in MW.\n\n## Where it stopped\n\nThe case is **not yet set**, and no plant was built, sized, simulated, checked or optimised. The blocking error is a data-format one, not an engineering one:\n\n> `demand.heating.power.file: row 1 time = '2027-01-01' has no offset; expected ISO 8601 with an offset or Z, or a time_zone for the file`\n> (same for the cooling file)\n\nThe demand CSVs carry bare local dates with no UTC offset, so gemini needs an IANA time zone for each series before it will accept them. That is a value I must not invent silently \u2014 it is a property of the site the load belongs to, and the requirements PDF did not give me one I could read out of the document in this run.\n\n## What is needed to finish (one answer unblocks everything)\n\n**The IANA time zone the 2027 daily demand is meant in** (e.g. `Europe/Zurich`, `Europe/Copenhagen`, `America/New_York`). I would record it as an assumption with its reason, then:\n\n1. `set_case` with `time_zone` on both series \u2192 case complete.\n2. `update_state`: the case's requirements as `case_requirement` items, plus my agent assumptions (backup policy, objective, evaluations, seed).\n3. Propose 2\u20136 materially different families (e.g. deep-geothermal doublet + heat pump + backup boiler; doublet with absorption chiller for cooling; doublet + dry cooler / free cooling; boiler-and-chiller-only reference), marking any that gemini cannot build as `blocked` with the reason.\n4. Per family: complete the plant file, `build_plant`, fix `issues`, `size_plant`, `simulate` the full year, `check_results`; record the first sized family's year as `design.start_result`.\n5. `optimize` the sized design (objective, evaluations, seed as my recorded assumptions), `simulate` the best, `check_results` it.\n6. With two or more buildable families, one `run_study` (`method=\"minimize\"`, `prepare=[\"size\"]`), keep the feasible design ranked first, simulate it for the whole year, and record `design.reference`, `design.result`, `design.family`, `design.schematic`, `design.alternatives` and `design.study.key`.\n\n## Status summary\n\n- **Design reference:** none yet \u2014 no `design/<name>` was stored.\n- **Full-year result reference:** none yet.\n- **`check_results` feasible:** not run.\n- **`optimize` feasible:** not run.\n- **Study ranking:** none.\n- **Reason not finished (domain: case/data):** the demand series have no time zone, so the case could not be completed; every downstream step (build, size, simulate, check, optimise) is blocked on it.\n\nGive me the time zone (or confirm one of the examples above) and I will run the full round \u2014 size, full-year simulate, check, optimise, re-simulate, and record the design with its study reference.", "tool_calls": [], "usage": {"input_tokens": 16903, "output_tokens": 967, "cost": 0.000886113, "cached_tokens": 16128}, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017"}
